    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Merge Intervals\n\nGiven an array of intervals where intervals[i] = [start_i, end_i], merge all overlapping intervals and return an array of the non-overlapping intervals that cover all the intervals in the input.\n\nExample: [[1,3],[2,6],[8,10],[15,18]] -> [[1,6],[8,10],[15,18]].\nConstraints: 1 <= len(intervals) <= 10^4.",
      "id": "m-1",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-01T05:05:54.935Z",
      "durationMs": 0
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "channel": "analysis",
      "content": "Edge cases to cover before submitting: empty input, single element, and the all-duplicates case.\n\nKey invariant: the data structure state after processing prefix i fully determines the answer for i+1.\n\nWriting the solution, then tracing it on the first example to confirm indices are handled correctly.",
      "id": "m-2",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-01T05:05:55.239Z",
      "durationMs": 13266,
      "stepIndex": 1
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "channel": "commentary",
